{"t":1788110418702,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d18e71c0309069b1b4be765a0bb318117acf832.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-66.66,17.97],[-66.64,18],[-66.64,17.98],[-66.58,17.96],[-66.48,17.99],[-66.39,17.94],[-66.32,17.98],[-66.25,17.93],[-66.26,17.94],[-66.21,17.96],[-66.17,17.94],[-66.21,17.94],[-66.21,17.93],[-66.15,17.94],[-66.16,17.93],[-65.82,18.01],[-65.82,17.52],[-66.68,17.5],[-66.66,17.97]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d18e71c0309069b1b4be765a0bb318117acf832.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d18e71c0309069b1b4be765a0bb318117acf832.001.1","areaDesc":"Caribbean Waters of Puerto Rico from 10 NM to 17N, including the Coastal Waters of Saint Croix; Coastal Waters of Southern Puerto Rico out 10 NM","geocode":{"SAME":["075733","075735"],"UGC":["AMZ733","AMZ735"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AMZ733","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AMZ735"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-30T12:40:00-04:00","effective":"2026-08-30T12:40:00-04:00","onset":"2026-08-30T12:40:00-04:00","expires":"2026-08-30T13:30:00-04:00","ends":"2026-08-30T13:30:00-04:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS San Juan PR","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued August 30 at 12:40PM AST until August 30 at 1:30PM AST by NWS San Juan PR","description":"SMWSJU\n\nThe National Weather Service in San Juan has issued a\n\n* Special Marine Warning for...\nCaribbean waters of Puerto Rico from 10 NM to 17N, including the\ncoastal waters of Saint Croix...\nCoastal Waters of Southern Puerto Rico out 10 NM...\n\n* Until 130 PM AST.\n\n* At 1240 PM AST, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing\nwaterspouts was located over over the waters south of southeastern\nPuerto Rico, moving west at 15 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts and wind gusts 34 knots or greater.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally\nhazardous seas. Small craft could be damaged in briefly\nhigher winds and suddenly higher waves.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nMainly open waters of Caribbean waters of Puerto Rico from 10 NM to\n17N, including the coastal waters of Saint Croix and Coastal Waters\nof Southern Puerto Rico out 10 NM.","instruction":"Move to safe harbor immediately as gusty winds and high waves are\nexpected.\n\nThunderstorms can produce sudden waterspouts. Waterspouts can easily\noverturn boats and create locally hazardous seas. Seek safe harbor\nimmediately.\n\nFrequent lightning is occurring with this storm. If caught on the\nopen water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded\nmetal objects.\n\nReport severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather\nService.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SMWSJU"],"WMOidentifier":["WHCA52 TJSJ 301640"],"maxWindGust":["34 knots"],"maxHailSize":["0.00"],"waterspoutDetection":["POSSIBLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.TJSJ.MA.W.0021.260830T1640Z-260830T1730Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T13:30:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SMW"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8f8e04e3194ea99a680df2f24a964cc9d3d3e12b.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-87.61,39.13],[-87.48,38.99],[-87.5,38.86],[-87.56,38.85],[-87.59,38.98],[-87.68,39.13],[-87.61,39.13]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8f8e04e3194ea99a680df2f24a964cc9d3d3e12b.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8f8e04e3194ea99a680df2f24a964cc9d3d3e12b.001.1","areaDesc":"Crawford, IL; Lawrence, IL; Knox, IN; Sullivan, IN","geocode":{"SAME":["017033","017101","018083","018153"],"UGC":["ILC033","ILC101","INC083","INC153"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ILC033","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ILC101","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/INC083","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/INC153"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a43560fddf6a3a82ffea67dc14c36f61179d0bd.002.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a43560fddf6a3a82ffea67dc14c36f61179d0bd.002.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-29T17:29:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-30T09:10:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-30T09:10:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-30T09:10:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-30T21:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-31T13:00:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Indianapolis IN","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 30 at 9:10AM CDT until August 31 at 1:00PM CDT by NWS Indianapolis IN","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Indiana...\nIllinois...\n\nWabash River at Riverton\n\n.Minor flooding continues on the Wabash River at Riverton. The river\nhas crested. Flooding is expected come to an end on the Wabash later\ntonight.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Riverton.\n\n* WHEN...Until late Sunday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 16.0 feet, Some agricultural lands underwater.  A few\nrural roads in Crawford County, Illinois close as water backs up\nMinnow Slough.  High water affects campground at Leaverton Park in\nPalestine.  A few private roads near the Gill Township levee in\nSullivan County may flood.  Water level is at the top of most\nmakeshift levees.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:00 AM CDT /9:00 AM EDT/ Sunday the stage was 16.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 10.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage just\nafter midnight tonight and continue falling to 4.7 feet\nWednesday, September 09.\n- Flood stage is 15.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 915 PM CDT /1015 PM\nEDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 301410"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL MONDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KIND.FL.W.0162.000000T0000Z-260831T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-31T13:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f12e54866dbe297df5336b1953067bd10aeed14.003.1,2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.55513f7e9c408f5bc1ea8c3d4b8ca021151f81f3.002.1,2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d6d2ad6897bfc2053b7ba54c44a8a9b438cb92a.002.1,2026-08-28T09:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.004.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6315cb2dc8d0f54eaa778ad01fb00cd0c181d340.003.1,2026-08-27T10:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.370c270d7d1b162addcf02dc7258854c454ad061.003.1,2026-08-26T13:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.12919d77a71ad3fa4d2d46fe4c889e8395a827c1.005.1,2026-08-26T09:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.21fed40f8a4270468743863bc5d2282950a3b72d.006.1,2026-08-25T13:12:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.966efdc66b3086f5aa2b21cb1cfbfa88e06cea3